# A write through a path to a number field checks its value's kind as any number place does: `b\v: "x"` (v an int of
# the Box b) went out as C storing the text's pointer into the int -- nothing typed a path write's value.  Refused at
# the value, in the words of the kind rule.
Box:
    int: v 0
end: Box
fn: peek () int
    Box: b
    b\v: "x"
    return: b\v
end: peek
int: r 0
r: peek()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
